### Summary of Goal Model

- **G1** is the top-level goal, decomposed into **G2** (food delivery) and **G3** (dish retrieval) with an **AND** relationship.
- **G2** is further decomposed into **G2.1** (direct delivery) and **G2.2** (tray fetching) with an **OR** relationship.
- **G2.2** is decomposed into **G2.2.1** (inpatient), **G2.2.2** (companion), **G2.2.3** (nurse), and **G2.2.4** (another robot) with an **OR** relationship.
- **G3** is decomposed into **G3.1** (unassisted), **G3.2** (with another robot), **G3.3** (with human), and **G3.4** (signal) with an **OR** relationship.
- Each task is linked to its respective goal with an **AND** or **OR** relationship based on the goal's decomposition.

This goal model provides a clear hierarchical structure for the multi-robot system to execute the food delivery and dish retrieval mission effectively.
